				},
				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "When making a business case for a migration, there can be incentives to underestimate the cost of migrating. People like to work with modern technology, that they don't perceive as being a dead end for their career. The sunk costs effect is real, as soon as a project is started there is loss of face involved in stopping it, and it is often easier to make more time and money available. "
			},
			{
				"__type" : "textSnippet",
				"children" : {
